Hi Suraj Sir,

I validated analytics.collections_bad_debt_mv against the Collections Raw_Dat=
a Sheet. tenure_days does not follow the business rule, so it does not match.=
 Could you please pick this up and update the DAG?

SUMMARY OF THE PROBLEM
- Rule: tenure should be counted only up to the driven week end (hissab_week =
- 1).
- The DAG today counts up to the Sunday of the hisaab week (hissab_week + 6).=
 For active partners, tenure comes out about 7 days too high.
- Only 11.3% of rows match the rule today, across 9 weeks (10 Aug - 5 Oct, 10=
2,909 partners).
- If the 7-day gap is ignored, 92.2% match. The remaining misses are in older=
 weeks, where driver_profile changed after those weeks were built. Those week=
s need a backfill.

WHAT NEEDS TO CHANGE IN THE DAG
Replace the current tenure_days logic with the CTE below and join it on (hiss=
ab_week, partner_etm). <mv base rows> stands for the per-week, per-partner ba=
se CTE the DAG already builds.

tenure_fix as (
  select m.hissab_week, m.partner_etm,
         coalesce(sum(least(coalesce(dp.end_date::date, m.hissab_week - 1), m=
.hissab_week - 1)
                      - dp.start_date::date + 1)
                  filter (where dp.start_date::date <=3D m.hissab_week - 1), =
0) as tenure_days
  from <mv base rows> m
  left join fleet_driver   fd on fd.employee_id =3D m.partner_etm
  left join driver_profile dp on dp.driver_id  =3D fd.id
  group by m.hissab_week, m.partner_etm
)
-- final select: tenure_fix.tenure_days as tenure_days

Tenure is the sum of all driver_profile stints (end - start + 1). The running=
 stint is cut at the driven week end, and stints that start later are not cou=
nted. fleet_driver.employee_id is unique, so the join does not double count.

STEPS
1. Make the change on a branch in EverestFleetOrg/scripts and raise a PR.
2. Test on week 2026-09-28 first. I expect about 10,504 of 12,594 rows to cha=
nge, by -5.4 days on average.
3. Merge, publish, and trigger the DAG in Airflow.
4. Backfill older weeks if the DAG only rebuilds recent ones.
5. Run the check query below. "different" should be 0 for every week.

with t as (
  select m.hissab_week, m.id, m.tenure_days,
         coalesce(sum(least(coalesce(dp.end_date::date, m.hissab_week - 1), m=
.hissab_week - 1) - dp.start_date::date + 1)
                  filter (where dp.start_date::date <=3D m.hissab_week - 1), =
0) as logic
  from analytics.collections_bad_debt_mv m
  left join fleet_driver   fd on fd.employee_id =3D m.partner_etm
  left join driver_profile dp on dp.driver_id  =3D fd.id
  where m.hissab_week >=3D '2026-08-10'
  group by m.hissab_week, m.id, m.tenure_days
)
select hissab_week, count(*) as rows,
       count(*) filter (where tenure_days is distinct from logic) as different
from t group by 1 order by 1;

The full details and week-wise numbers are in this doc: https://claude.ai/cod=
e/artifact/25af8393-1df4-482b-8729-cee1062d5622

Once the DAG has run, I will re-validate against the Sheet and confirm.

Thanks,
Mithun

